## DO NOT

1. DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for the SSIM2 recovery — mechanism is
   structural (1× → 2× DC integer precision, libjxl `nl_dc` parity).
2. DO NOT extend `extra_dc_precision = 1` to effort ≥ 8 — libjxl drops
   to 1× precision at speed_tier ≥ kFalcon (effort ≥ 8) because the
   butteraugli loop owns DC refinement above that threshold. A widening
   would diverge in the OPPOSITE direction from libjxl.
3. DO NOT default-flip on JPEG re-encoding path — `frame.rs:549` is
   explicitly kept at extra_dc_precision = 0 because JPEG re-encoding
   has no encoder-side DC quantization (DC values come directly from
   the JPEG bitstream).
4. DO NOT roll back the symmetric `dc_mul` multiplication in
   `reconstruct.rs` — without it, the encoder-side buttloop comparison
   would see DC values 2× too large after dequant, throwing off
   convergence on the e≥8 path.
5. DO NOT respawn for "e9 cluster cells didn't close" — those live on
   buttloop convergence / W44-105 chain; the Phase 5 DC quant fix is
   structurally orthogonal at e≥8 where extra_dc_precision = 0.

## Follow-on candidates (NOT in Phase 5 scope)

- **Phase 6 / PRIORITY 2**: match libjxl's `QuantizeWP` shape on the
  `kWPFixedDC` path (deadzone 0.62, WP-prediction-relative residual,
  snap-to-even for residuals > |2|). Phase 4 memo §3 documents this
  as the secondary mechanism; Phase 5 measurement shows it would only
  affect the residual e9 cluster cells (where bytes drift remains
  -3 to -7% vs cjxl), so EV is bounded but real.
- **240-cell wider corpus regression sweep**: confirm zero FIXED→OPEN
  flips outside the cluster. Defer to a follow-on chunk; current
  measurement is internally consistent and the gate fires uniformly
  across all effort-≤7 cells per design.
